    mgr/DaemonServer: add explicit DaemonServer shutdown handling
    
    The mgr unit tests were experiencing segfaults and 'pure virtual method called'
    errors during rapid creation and destruction of DaemonServer objects. This
    occurred because the OpTracker's OpHistory background thread could still be
    running and accessing DaemonServer's op_tracker after DaemonServer began
    destruction, leading to use-after-free conditions.
    
    When DaemonServer's destructor runs, its members (including op_tracker) begin
    destruction, but the OpHistory thread may still be running and attempting to
    access the op_tracker that is being destroyed.
    
    Add an explicit shutdown() method to DaemonServer that stops the OpTracker's
    OpHistory thread before any member destruction begins. Call this from Mgr's
    destructor to ensure proper shutdown ordering. Use an atomic compare_exchange
    to make shutdown idempotent, allowing it to be safely called from both Mgr's
    destructor (preferred path) and DaemonServer's destructor (fallback).
    
    This establishes a clear shutdown lifecycle: Mgr calls server.shutdown() which
    stops the OpHistory thread, then DaemonServer's destructor runs and safely
    destroys op_tracker with no background threads accessing it.
    
    Fixes: https://tracker.ceph.com/issues/76334
    Signed-off-by: stzuraski898 <steven.zuraski@ibm.com>

